<title>SWITZERLAND: Ciba rights start trading at 100 Sfr.</title>
<headline>Ciba rights start trading at 100 Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rights for shares in Ciba Specialty Chemicals Holding Inc, being spun off from Novartis, started trading on the Swiss Exchange at 100 Swiss francs.</p>
<p>A bank consortium has fixed a floor price of 64 francs per right, representing a share price of 74 francs per registered share, for the rights, which are being issued to Novartis shareholders in a one-for-one rights issue.</p>
<p>The consortium will use the rights to buy shares for sale in a global offering with at least 300 million francs worth of shares. Share trading starts on March 13. -- Zurich +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
